{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:0.2", "PA_ja_58:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Āsīsavagga (The Chapter on Aspirations)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:0.4"], "en": "8. The Jātaka of the Three Qualities:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:1.1", "PA_ja_58:1.2"], "en": "“O Lord of Monkeys, he in whom these three qualities exist, just as they do in you—”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:1.3"], "en": "“Wisdom is the sun of the South;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:1.4"], "en": "he overcomes what has been seen.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_58:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the eighth Jātaka, the Tayodhamma Jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
